I will write the code that detects a horizontal separator (row of non-zero values) or a vertical separator (column of non-zero values). If a separator is found, it splits the grid into two parts (Top/Bottom or Left/Right) and applies a logical AND operation: output is 2 if both parts have non-zero values, and 0 otherwise. For the case of the test input, a vertical separator at column 4 (value 1) splits the grid into two 4x4 subgrids, which are then combined. For the demonstration input, the horizontal separator at row 13 is handled similarly. The dimension logic uses the minimum of the split parts' dimensions to ensure valid pairing.

